From 9599ef2586c0216db6fe6f1063ebd88b66481ae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:52:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix critical bugs and migrate SQLite -> PostgreSQL for Vercel

Deployment
- Switch Prisma datasource from SQLite to PostgreSQL. SQLite cannot run on
  Vercel's read-only serverless filesystem, so every DB query returned HTTP 500
  and login was impossible. Add pooled DATABASE_URL + DIRECT_URL for migrations.
- Give all money columns explicit Decimal(10,2) precision.
- Regenerate migrations for Postgres; add scripts/migrate-sqlite-to-postgres.js
  to carry existing guests/bookings/payments across.
- Run prisma generate && migrate deploy during build so tables exist on deploy.
- Add .env.example and DEPLOY.md; stop tracking prisma/*.db.

Security
- Fix auth bypass: the middleware matcher excluded any path starting with
  'guest', so /guests and /api/guests/lookup were fully public, exposing the
  guest register (names, mobiles, addresses, ID proof numbers). Anchor the
  exclusions so only /guest/<token> and /api/guest/* stay public.
- Require the room QR token when a guest rates a service request; previously
  any visitor could rate arbitrary request IDs.
- Scope guest request history to the current stay so the next occupant of a
  room can't read the previous guest's requests.
- Require an authenticated manager/owner for the QR base-URL settings endpoint.
- Validate uploads (type + 8MB limit) and derive the extension from the MIME
  type instead of the attacker-controlled filename.

Booking logic
- A reservation weeks away no longer marks a room RESERVED immediately, which
  had made the room unsellable for tonight. Introduce syncRoomStatus() as the
  single source of truth, deriving status from live bookings with a 24h
  look-ahead, and use it from every mutation.
- Walk-in check-in now checks for date overlap instead of the room's current
  status flag.
- Fix check-out leaving a room AVAILABLE when it still held a reservation.
- Fix delay-arrival dragging a future reservation back to today, destroying the
  booking date; only the time of day now moves.
- Don't write a zero/negative payment row when settling an over-paid booking.

Correctness
- Fix cascading-render lint errors in the nav badges via a shared
  usePendingRequestCount hook.
- Replace require() with dynamic import in firebase-admin and stop retrying
  initialisation on every notification.
